<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ar6-cid#CoastalFlood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flooding driven by episodic high coastal water levels that result from a combination of relative sea level rise, tides, storm surge and wave setup." .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ar6-cid#FireWeather> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Weather conditions conducive to triggering and sustaining wildfires, usually based on a set of indicators and combinations of indicators including temperature, soil moisture, humidity and wind. Fire weather does not include the presence or absence of fuel load. Note: distinct from wildfire occurrence and area burned." .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ar6-cid#OceanAcidity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ar6-cid#CID-category> .
